<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Union of Krewo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1385</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Union of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kreva">Krewo</a> was an agreement of 1385 under which Grand Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/w-adys-aw-ii-jagie-o">Jogaila</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> agreed to accept Catholic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> and marry <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jadwiga-of-poland">Queen Jadwiga</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, becoming King of Poland. It created a personal union between Poland and Lithuania. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a> treat it as the starting point of the union that culminated in the Commonwealth.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/union-of-krewo.jpg" alt="Union of Krewo" width="320" height="195" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: en:Jogaila · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Union_of_Krewo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
